#! rnews 542
Path: summer98.example!not-for-mail
From: skylark <skylark@summer98.example>
Newsgroups: alt.games.homebrew
Subject: Last Light - a small game about a lighthouse (artist wanted)
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 1998 22:14:05 -0700
Message-ID: <ll-0001.skylark@summer98.example>
X-Fixture: fictional sample for Resurrection V5
Lines: 6

I am making a little game about a seaside town with a lighthouse keeper
called Theo. The light does not work yet. Neither does most of the game.

I can code and I can write music. I cannot draw a seagull. Anyone?

-- sky
#! rnews 533
Path: summer98.example!not-for-mail
From: junebug <june@inkwell.example>
Newsgroups: alt.games.homebrew
Subject: Re: Last Light - a small game about a lighthouse (artist wanted)
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 1998 10:02:44 -0700
Message-ID: <junebug.19980419.1@inkwell.example>
References: <ll-0001.skylark@summer98.example>
X-Fixture: fictional sample for Resurrection V5
Lines: 6

> I cannot draw a seagull.

I can draw you a seagull. I can draw you the whole town, and I will
write the people in it. Theo needs a beard. Also a baker.

-- june
